{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.CptD6D7D8Closure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.CptD6D7D8Closure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cptClosure_of_components","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cptClosure_of_components","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.lean#L106-L126","doc":"**CPT closure follows from its three components.**\n\nIf each of charge conjugation, parity and time reversal preserves the Markov\ntrace, then so does `C ∘ P ∘ T`.  This is the reduction the `.md` asserts\nwhen it says the three components *\"collectively constitute the\nconjecture\"*, and it is derived rather than assumed.\n\nWhat remains open is each component hypothesis — that the colour-sheet\nflavour swap, the braid-diagram mirror and Markov-trace word reversal are the\nright realisations and are individually trace-preserving. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTClosure.cpt_trace_preserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTClosure.cpt_trace_preserved","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.lean#L104-L104","doc":"**The conjecture itself** (joint closure of the three symmetries): the\nCPT composite preserves the Markov trace on every closed braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTClosure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTClosure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTClosure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTClosure","kind":"class","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.lean#L87-L104","doc":"The CPT-closure compound conjecture, as a class over the objects it is\nabout.\n\n`B` is the closed-braid representative space, `markovTrace : B → R` the Jones\ninvariant valued in the generic coefficient ring `R` — canonically\n$\\mathbb{Z}[q, q^{-1}]$, never `ℝ` — and `cptComposite` the joint `C · P · T`\naction.  All three are **parameters**, so a `[CPTClosure R B tr cpt]` binder\nis a hypothesis about the caller's trace and action.\n\nNo instance is supplied; the class *is* the conjecture. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure","label":"conj:cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_closure","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.lean#L76-L85","doc":"**The claim of `conj:cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure`**: the composite `C · P · T`\npreserves the Markov trace.\n\nNamed over caller-supplied data, **not asserted** — this is the conjecture.\nThe class below is its hypothesis-carrying form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.PreservesMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.PreservesMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-d6-d7-d8-closure.lean#L66-L74","doc":"**A symmetry action preserves the Markov trace**:\n`tr_M(f β) = tr_M(β)` for every closed-braid representative `β`.\n\nStated over a caller-supplied trace `tr` and action `f`.  This is the shape\neach of `C`, `P`, `T` is conjectured to have, and the shape their composite\nis conjectured to inherit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}